<title>UK: UniChem buys two pharmacies for 716,000 stg.</title>
<headline>UniChem buys two pharmacies for 716,000 stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drug wholesaler and retailer UniChem Plc said on Wednesday it bought two pharmacies in England for about 716,000 stg in stock.</p>
<p>UniChem said it would issue 126,259 UniChem ordinary shares worth 2.5543 stg each to buy I. Burt in Stansted and ADJ &amp; JC Holden Ltd in Haltwhistle.</p>
<p>The firm said the acquisition, together with consolidation of outlets in other areas, meant that its Moss Chemists division traded from 459 outlets in England, Scotland and Wales.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
